summary:
  An alarm nobody answered goes on counting as ringing after its half hour.

history:
  Somebody who has had the alarm's station on for half an hour is up, and
  an empty flat has nobody in it to wake. With no end to the ringing, a
  network that drops hours later and is not back within the knock's eight
  seconds ends in the tone, at the alarm's volume, until somebody comes
  home.

target:
  package/contents/ui/AlarmLogic.js

find:
      return nowMs - firedAtMs <= WAKE_WINDOW_MS;

replace:
      return nowMs - firedAtMs >= 0;

expect:
  Killed by tst_alarmlogic::test_an_alarm_rings_for_half_an_hour_from_its_fire.
  Line-neutral.
